        "slide": 1,
        "role": "cover",
        "subject": "A brass pillar balance on an ebonized base, standing on a chalk plinth. The beam is tilted down to the left. The left pan holds a tall polished brass stack and the right pan a shorter blued stack. A bevelled nickel needle crosses a chalk arc, and the dim city hall glazing sits behind in a navy field.",
        "visual_consequence": "Without the headline the beam leans toward the taller brass stack, and the two metals separate cleanly at feed size. One line is heavier than the other on the same instrument, and the heavier one is the brass.",
        "weakness": "None blocking. The hook 'A chatbot for Plano, and / Darwin AI beside it' sets in two lines inside the margins, ending short of the counter (r1c2). Its last line clears the dek cap height with a normal gap (r1c1). The dek ends about 300 native px above the beam's left end (r2c1), so no type crosses the balance. The cite and site lines sit on the plinth face, clear of the pan and base (r3c1, r3c2). The art is unchanged from my previous reading. The plinth face is still a warm lit band, the glazing still reads navy gray, and the dek's lower lines sit over the faint city hall silhouette, where they stay legible.",
